# .nxignore — what eden's project graph must never glob in.
#
# Eden carries `.devcontainer/`, `libs/` and `infrastructure/` as git submodules, and it builds
# ONE nx graph over the whole checkout. A submodule's TEST FIXTURES are not eden's projects, but
# a fixture that needs a `project.json` to be a realistic stand-in looks exactly like one.
#
# WHY THIS FILE HAS TO EXIST, rather than the submodules simply naming their fixtures well.
# A fixture `project.json` inside a submodule is invisible to BOTH repositories' gates:
#
#   - the submodule builds no nx graph, so its own CI cannot see the name. `.devcontainer`'s
#     `cmd_validate` runs `jq empty` over such a file and reads no field of it;
#   - eden never sees the file at all until its POINTER MOVES.
#
# So the first thing in the estate able to observe a collision is a submodule pointer bump — the
# worst place for it. gophersys/eden#14 carried 787 commits and zero TypeScript and died at
# `NX Failed to process project graph`, because `.devcontainer` had grown a SECOND `first`/`second`
# fixture pair in `40edaaf`. That bump SURFACED the defect and could not have caused it. Naming the
# fixtures uniquely (gophersys/.devcontainer#105) fixes THAT collision; this file is what makes the
# CLASS impossible, so the next fixture somebody adds in any of the three submodules cannot reach
# eden's graph at all.
#
# WHY THE PATTERNS END IN `project.json` INSTEAD OF EXCLUDING THE FIXTURE TREES WHOLE.
# `.nxignore` hides a path from nx completely — from project detection AND from the file-change
# reads behind `nx affected`. Excluding `**/testdata/` whole would therefore stop a change to a Go
# testdata file from marking its library affected, and the gate would quietly stop covering it.
# That is the FAIL-NOT-SKIP failure — a check believed to run that no longer does — traded in to
# fix a graph error. Hiding the `project.json` FILE alone removes the phantom project and leaves
# every other fixture file visible to affected, which is the whole intent and nothing more.
#
# EDEN'S OWN TREE IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT from this file. A duplicate project name that eden itself
# commits is caught by eden's own gate on the pull request that adds it. The submodules are the
# blind spot; eden is not.
#
# THIS FILE HAS A HOLDER: `bash .ci/ctl.sh graph-guard`, run by the `fast` job of on-pr.yml. A glob
# here that silently stopped matching would restore the whole defect class with nothing going red.
# The guard searches `fixtures?|testdata` — deliberately ONE case wider than the patterns below,
# which spell the singular `fixture/` out. If the two ever drift, the guard goes RED rather than
# the hole opening quietly, and that direction is the point.

.devcontainer/**/fixture/**/project.json
.devcontainer/**/fixtures/**/project.json
.devcontainer/**/testdata/**/project.json

libs/**/fixture/**/project.json
libs/**/fixtures/**/project.json
libs/**/testdata/**/project.json

infrastructure/**/fixture/**/project.json
infrastructure/**/fixtures/**/project.json
infrastructure/**/testdata/**/project.json
